{"id":"p1x4","name":"Deduplicate rides and driver gaps","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","rides_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Rides are sent to the data platform by two systems, <code>\"app\"</code> and <code>\"backoffice\"</code>, so the same ride can arrive several times. <code>rides_df</code> has the columns:</p>\n<ul><li><code>ride_id</code> - the ID of the ride (string);</li><li><code>driver_id</code> - the driver (string);</li><li><code>started_at</code> - when the ride started (timestamp);</li><li><code>source</code> - <code>\"app\"</code> or <code>\"backoffice\"</code>;</li><li><code>received_at</code> - when the platform received this copy (timestamp).</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to:</p>\n<ol><li>keep one copy of each <code>ride_id</code>: the one with the earliest <code>received_at</code>; if two copies were received at the same time, keep the one whose <code>source</code> comes first alphabetically;</li><li>for each driver, compute <code>gap_minutes</code>: the number of whole minutes between the <code>started_at</code> of the ride and the <code>started_at</code> of the previous ride of the same driver (null for the first ride of a driver).</li></ol>\n<p>Return <code>ride_id</code>, <code>driver_id</code>, <code>started_at</code>, <code>source</code> and <code>gap_minutes</code> (integer), sorted by <code>driver_id</code>, then <code>started_at</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>rides_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>ride_id</th><th>driver_id</th><th>started_at</th><th>source</th><th>received_at</th></tr><tr><td>R1</td><td>D1</td><td>2026-03-01 08:00:00</td><td>app</td><td>2026-03-01 08:30:00</td></tr><tr><td>R1</td><td>D1</td><td>2026-03-01 08:00:00</td><td>backoffice</td><td>2026-03-01 08:10:00</td></tr><tr><td>R2</td><td>D1</td><td>2026-03-01 08:45:30</td><td>app</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td></tr><tr><td>R3</td><td>D2</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td><td>backoffice</td><td>2026-03-01 09:20:00</td></tr><tr><td>R3</td><td>D2</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td><td>app</td><td>2026-03-01 09:20:00</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>ride_id</th><th>driver_id</th><th>started_at</th><th>source</th><th>gap_minutes</th></tr><tr><td>R1</td><td>D1</td><td>2026-03-01 08:00:00</td><td>backoffice</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>R2</td><td>D1</td><td>2026-03-01 08:45:30</td><td>app</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>R3</td><td>D2</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td><td>app</td><td>null</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, rides_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return rides_df\n","hints":["Étape 1 : row_number() sur Window.partitionBy(\"ride_id\").orderBy(\"received_at\", \"source\"), garde rn = 1. dropDuplicates ne choisit pas quelle copie il garde.","Étape 2 : F.lag(\"started_at\").over(Window.partitionBy(\"driver_id\").orderBy(\"started_at\")). Différence en secondes avec F.unix_timestamp, divise par 60, cast(\"int\")."],"summary_fr":"Une course peut être envoyée plusieurs fois. Garde la copie reçue en premier (received_at le plus petit, puis source alphabétique). Ensuite, pour chaque chauffeur, calcule les minutes depuis sa course précédente (null pour la première). Trie par driver_id puis started_at.","tags":["Window","row_number","lag","dédoublonnage"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"rides_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"ride_id STRING, driver_id STRING, started_at TIMESTAMP, source STRING, received_at TIMESTAMP","rows":[["R1","D1","2026-03-01 08:00:00","app","2026-03-01 08:30:00"],["R1","D1","2026-03-01 08:00:00","backoffice","2026-03-01 08:10:00"],["R2","D1","2026-03-01 08:45:30","app","2026-03-01 09:00:00"],["R3","D2","2026-03-01 09:00:00","backoffice","2026-03-01 09:20:00"],["R3","D2","2026-03-01 09:00:00","app","2026-03-01 09:20:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["ride_id","driver_id","started_at","source","gap_minutes"],"rows":[["R1","D1","2026-03-01 08:00:00","backoffice",null],["R2","D1","2026-03-01 08:45:30","app",45],["R3","D2","2026-03-01 09:00:00","app",null]]}},{"input":{"rides_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"ride_id STRING, driver_id STRING, started_at TIMESTAMP, source STRING, received_at TIMESTAMP","rows":[["X","D9","2026-03-02 23:50:00","app","2026-03-03 00:00:00"],["Y","D9","2026-03-03 00:20:00","app","2026-03-03 00:30:00"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["ride_id","driver_id","started_at","source","gap_minutes"],"rows":[["X","D9","2026-03-02 23:50:00","app",null],["Y","D9","2026-03-03 00:20:00","app",30]]}}],"hidden_n":5,"hidden":"","solution":""}